{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:26:59Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 19, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "=== design-attempt1.output ===\nThe spec confirms this: backend-only persistence change, no request/response shape changes, explicit non-goal \"No frontend change,\" and \"Not affected: `frontend/` (entire directory).\" There's no screen, component, or user-visible state for me to design \u2014 persistence is invisible at the API boundary, so there's nothing for a UX design doc to cover.\n\nI'm not writing `docs/design.md` for this one \u2014 this is a no-op stage, exactly as the spec anticipated. This should go straight to the developer stage with the existing `docs/spec.md`.=== design-attempt2.output ===\n`docs/design.md` is now written for Taiga #5, confirming this stage is a no-op: the feature is entirely backend-internal (write-on-mutation, load-on-construct), no route shapes, no frontend files, and no new user-visible state are introduced, so there's nothing for the ux-designer role to specify. It traces each acceptance criterion to why no design element applies and hands off directly to the developer stage.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01K8Xw39TUbEQcjC3EmvJ7fs", "session_id": "ab249e80-4d7e-43b0-9f8b-5d4464bab442"}}
