{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:27:21Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 47, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tConfirmed: only `docs/spec.md` and `docs/design.md` are modified so far; no backend code changes exist yet from a parallel developer, and my scope is explicitly frontend.\n2\t\n3\tBoth the spec and design docs are unambiguous and consistent: this feature (Taiga #5, backend disk persistence for `TaskStore`) is entirely internal to `backend/app/store.py`. The spec's \"Affected areas\" states plainly *\"Not affected: `frontend/` (entire directory)\"*, and the design doc confirms zero frontend surface \u2014 no new routes, no response-shape changes, no new UI states. There is no work in my assigned frontend scope for this story.\n4\t\n5\tPer my role's discipline (minimal diff, faithful scope, don't invent work), I'm not going to touch `frontend/` since there's nothing the spec asks for there \u2014 adding anything would be scope creep on a well-specified backend-only feature.\n6\t\n7\t**Handoff:** No frontend changes required for Taiga #5. `frontend/src/api.js` and all components already call the existing `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tasks*` endpoints and render whatever comes back \u2014 since the backend's response shapes are unchanged (per spec non-goals: `backend/app/models.py` untouched), no frontend file needs modification, and none was modified. This mirrors the ux-designer stage's own no-op finding. The reviewer stage can verify this by diffing `frontend/` (empty) and confirming `frontend/src/api.js` needs no changes to work correctly against the persisted-tasks backend.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013XWGL3bBaga1rAW8G3vSn4", "session_id": "ab249e80-4d7e-43b0-9f8b-5d4464bab442"}}
