{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:28:31Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 127, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t## Handoff\n2\t\n3\t**Fixed in `backend/app/store.py`:**\n4\t\n5\t- **#2 (non-atomic write)** \u2014 `_save()` now writes to a `.tmp` sibling file and `os.replace()`s it into place (store.py:44-49). A kill mid-write leaves the temp file torn, never the real `tasks.json`, so a restart after an interrupted save still loads the last good snapshot.\n6\t- **#3 (silent corruption)** \u2014 `_load()` now catches `FileNotFoundError` separately (silent, as before \u2014 that's the benign \"no file yet\" case) and logs `logger.warning(...)` for every other exception (parse errors, shape mismatches) before starting empty (store.py:29-40), so a wiped/corrupted data file is now discoverable in the server logs instead of indistinguishable from first-run.\n7\t- **#4 (concurrent-thread races)** \u2014 left as-is per the review's own verdict: explicitly not blocking, filed as a follow-up rather than in scope here.\n8\t\n9\t`cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2014 **30 passed**, confirmed in this session.\n10\t\n11\t**Blocked, not applied \u2014 needs your attention:**\n12\t\n13\t- **`.gitignore`** (must-fix #1): every attempt to add `backend/data/` \u2014 via Edit, Write, and a Bash shell redirect \u2014 was rejected by this session's permission system with \"you haven't granted it yet,\" repeated across five separate tries. This is the one **blocking** finding and it's still open in the working tree.\n14\t- **`backend/tests/test_persistence.py`**: I tried to add one small test (`test_save_does_not_leave_a_temp_file_behind`, asserting no stray `.tmp` file survives a save) to cover the atomic-write fix directly \u2014 same permission rejection, twice.\n15\t\n16\tBoth are one paragraph/one function, ready to apply \u2014 I just can't get either file write approved in this session. Someone with interactive approval needs to either grant the edit or apply these two small diffs by hand:\n17\t\n18\t```diff\n19\t--- a/.gitignore\n20\t+++ b/.gitignore\n21\t@@\n22\t .pytest_cache/\n23\t+backend/data/\n24\t```\n25\t\n26\t```diff\n27\t--- a/backend/tests/test_persistence.py\n28\t+++ b/backend/tests/test_persistence.py\n29\t@@\n30\t+def test_save_does_not_leave_a_temp_file_behind(tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n31\t+    data_file = tmp_path / \"tasks.json\"\n32\t+    monkeypatch.setenv(\"TASKS_DATA_FILE\", str(data_file))\n33\t+\n34\t+    store = TaskStore()\n35\t+    store.add(\"write atomically\")\n36\t+\n37\t+    assert list(tmp_path.iterdir()) == [data_file]\n38\t+\n39\t+\n40\t def test_data_directory_is_created_on_first_write(tmp_path, monkeypatch):\n41\t```\n42\t\n43\tNot marking this complete: must-fix #1 is still unresolved in the actual repo, even though the fix content is fully specified above.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01EEZe2uno2A6G5sa7rJU5JN", "session_id": "ab249e80-4d7e-43b0-9f8b-5d4464bab442"}}
